$json2texts — expand JSON array in texts[] into separate text links

SUMMARY
  Parses each texts[] file as a JSON array and writes one texts[] link per
  element (or a single joined file). Input JSON texts are replaced, not kept.

SYNTAX
  $json2texts
  $json2texts(field='text')
  $json2texts(join=1)

INPUT
  texts[] — each file should contain a JSON array, e.g. from $search:
    [{"url": "https://…", "text": "snippet"}, …]

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one .txt per array element (string values used as-is; objects
            use field= or common keys: text, snippet, description, title).

ARGUMENTS
  field=  — object key to extract (default text)
  join=1  — merge all elements into one texts[] file (\\n\\n separated)

EXAMPLE
  @search_birds: $search -> $json2texts -> $llm

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
